{"id":169,"date":"2026-07-09T14:30:49","date_gmt":"2026-07-09T14:30:49","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/localhost:8181\/wood-stove-downstairs-heat-pump-everywhere-else-a-warren-combination-that-works\/"},"modified":"2026-07-14T19:43:56","modified_gmt":"2026-07-14T19:43:56","slug":"wood-stove-downstairs-heat-pump-everywhere-else-a-warren-combination-that-works","status":"publish","type":"page","link":"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wood-stove-downstairs-heat-pump-everywhere-else-a-warren-combination-that-works\/","title":{"rendered":"Your Heat Pump Won&#8217;t Survive Warren&#8217;s Plateau Winters"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<div class=\"wp-block-media-text alignfull has-media-on-the-right s-hero-split wp-elements-6e9173f254559b414a8196e99f379310\" style=\"grid-template-columns:auto 50%\"><div class=\"wp-block-media-text__content\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-element-heading s-hero-split__text wp-block-heading\">Heat that survives Warren winters.<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Warren&#039;s winters hit harder than anywhere else in northwestern Pennsylvania, and your outdoor HVAC equipment takes the full brunt of Allegheny Plateau cold.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-buttons-is-layout-35f06ea7 wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"\/contact\/\">Book the Assessment<\/a><\/div>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div><figure class=\"wp-block-media-text__media\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"678\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/6791940537_40b7d0ac00_b.jpg\" alt=\"boiler pipes heating system\" class=\"wp-image-187\" style=\"object-fit:cover;height:100%\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/6791940537_40b7d0ac00_b.jpg 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/6791940537_40b7d0ac00_b-300x199.jpg 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/6791940537_40b7d0ac00_b-768x509.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--stock\" title=\"&quot;20110719-RD-LSC-0205&quot; by USDAgov, BY, via Openverse\">Stock<\/span><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"s-trust-bar\"><div class=\"s-trust__item\">15+ Years Serving PA<\/div><div class=\"s-trust__item\">Licensed &amp; Insured<\/div><div class=\"s-trust__item\">Same-Day Emergency<\/div><div class=\"s-trust__item\">Local to Your Area<\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-media-text\" style=\"grid-template-columns:50% auto\"><figure class=\"wp-block-media-text__media\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"683\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-minisplit-1-1024x683.png\" alt=\"minisplit - professional HVAC service photo\" class=\"wp-image-1481\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-minisplit-1-1024x683.png 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-minisplit-1-300x200.png 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-minisplit-1-768x512.png 768w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-minisplit-1.png 1536w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--ai\" title=\"AI-generated (gpt-image-1)\">AI<\/span><\/figure><div class=\"wp-block-media-text__content\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Why heat pumps struggle here.<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Heat pumps are efficient in moderate climates, but Warren pushes them to operational limits. As temperatures drop below freezing, a heat pump&#039;s capacity decreases dramatically. By zero degrees, most standard units deliver only a fraction of rated capacity, and electric resistance backup strips take over, consuming electricity at rates that make oil heat look economical.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Modern cold-climate heat pumps perform better, maintaining capacity to negative temperatures, but they cost significantly more and still need backup heating for Warren&#039;s coldest nights. Many homeowners benefit from hybrid systems pairing a heat pump with a furnace\u2014using the pump for shoulder seasons and mild winter days while relying on the furnace when temperatures drop below twenty degrees. Defrost cycles add another layer of complexity.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">When outdoor coils ice up\u2014constantly in Warren&#039;s humid cold\u2014the system reverses to melt frost, temporarily blowing cold air inside. In drafty older homes, each defrost cycle feels like the heat quit entirely. Proper auxiliary heat coverage closes that gap, but undersized backup systems leave occupants noticing temperature swings.<\/p>\n\n<\/div><\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group alignfull s-band s-band--sand has-tint-background-color has-background has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-08713647 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:6rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:6rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What Warren HVAC demands.<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Proper system design for Warren starts with a Manual J heat load calculation using actual design temperature around negative five degrees Fahrenheit\u2014not generic Pennsylvania averages. Every wall, window, door, and ceiling gets factored in, along with insulation values and air leakage.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list s-icon-list\">\n<li>Oversized furnaces short-cycle and create temperature swings even when the thermostat reads seventy<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Undersized systems run constantly during cold snaps, struggling to maintain comfort while driving up energy costs<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Ductwork sized for milder climates can&#039;t deliver required airflow when outdoor temperatures plunge below zero<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Insulation upgrades in attics and rim joists can reduce required furnace capacity by twenty percent, allowing smaller more efficient equipment<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Whole-house humidification improves comfort at lower thermostat settings and reduces heating costs by making air feel warmer<\/li>\n\n<\/ul>\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group alignfull s-band s-band--ink has-contrast-background-color has-background has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-08713647 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:6rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:6rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group alignfull s-band s-band--sand has-tint-background-color has-background has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-08713647 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:6rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:6rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Services built for extreme cold.<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns alignwide s-feature-row is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-794e3cfa wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-card s-feature-card is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-medium s-feature-card__img\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"683\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/300873227_7224777c44_b.jpg\" alt=\"boiler pipes heating system\" class=\"wp-image-186\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/300873227_7224777c44_b.jpg 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/300873227_7224777c44_b-300x200.jpg 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/300873227_7224777c44_b-768x512.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--stock\" title=\"&quot;Pipes&quot; by twoshortplanks, BY-SA, via Openverse\">Stock<\/span><\/figure>\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Furnace replacement &amp; sizing<\/h3>\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Proper Manual J calculations ensure your furnace delivers full output at Warren&#039;s design temperature.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-card s-feature-card is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-medium s-feature-card__img\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"683\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-2-1024x683.png\" alt=\"technician - professional HVAC service photo\" class=\"wp-image-1476\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-2-1024x683.png 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-2-300x200.png 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-2-768x512.png 768w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-2.png 1536w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--ai\" title=\"AI-generated (gpt-image-1)\">AI<\/span><\/figure>\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Cold-climate heat pump installation<\/h3>\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Models rated for sub-zero operation with integrated backup heat for the coldest weeks.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-card s-feature-card is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-medium s-feature-card__img\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"683\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-furnace-1-1024x683.png\" alt=\"furnace - professional HVAC service photo\" class=\"wp-image-1477\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-furnace-1-1024x683.png 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-furnace-1-300x200.png 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-furnace-1-768x512.png 768w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-furnace-1.png 1536w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--ai\" title=\"AI-generated (gpt-image-1)\">AI<\/span><\/figure>\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Hybrid heating systems<\/h3>\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Heat pump and furnace paired with smart controls that switch seamlessly between heat sources.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-card s-feature-card is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-medium s-feature-card__img\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"1024\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-furnace-1.png\" alt=\"furnace - professional HVAC service photo\" class=\"wp-image-1757\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-furnace-1.png 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-furnace-1-300x300.png 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-furnace-1-150x150.png 150w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-furnace-1-768x768.png 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--ai\" title=\"AI-generated (gemini-2.5-flash-image)\">AI<\/span><\/figure>\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Emergency backup heating<\/h3>\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Wood stoves, pellet stoves, and generator-backed systems for power outages that last days.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-card s-feature-card is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-medium s-feature-card__img\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"1024\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-1.png\" alt=\"technician - professional HVAC service photo\" class=\"wp-image-1755\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-1.png 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-1-300x300.png 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-1-150x150.png 150w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-1-768x768.png 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--ai\" title=\"AI-generated (gemini-2.5-flash-image)\">AI<\/span><\/figure>\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Condensate and drainage fixes<\/h3>\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Interior drain routing that prevents freeze damage to high-efficiency furnaces and heat pumps.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-card s-feature-card is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-medium s-feature-card__img\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"1024\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-2.png\" alt=\"technician - professional HVAC service photo\" class=\"wp-image-1756\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-2.png 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-2-300x300.png 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-2-150x150.png 150w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-2-768x768.png 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--ai\" title=\"AI-generated (gemini-2.5-flash-image)\">AI<\/span><\/figure>\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Equipment protection &amp; placement<\/h3>\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Elevated condenser stands, wildlife guards, and strategic positioning that survives snow load and ice dams.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-media-text has-media-on-the-right\" style=\"grid-template-columns:auto 50%\"><div class=\"wp-block-media-text__content\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Snow, ice, and wildlife damage.<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Warren&#039;s location near Allegheny National Forest means wildlife isn&#039;t just a rural problem. Raccoons, squirrels, and porcupines investigate outdoor HVAC equipment, chewing wiring insulation, nesting in condenser cabinets, and damaging components. A single raccoon destroys a condenser&#039;s fan motor by bending blades or gnawing control wires. Squirrels chew refrigerant lines looking for minerals, causing leaks that require expensive repairs. Snow and ice create equally serious problems.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Condensers placed too close to rooflines get buried by avalanches of sliding snow, bending coil fins and straining fan assemblies. Units on north-facing walls face the worst drifting and spend months in shade that prevents melting. Ice dams form around the base, trapping condensate and meltwater that refreezes into solid blocks.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The best installations place condensers on south or east sides of the house, elevated at least eighteen inches above grade, with generous clearance from roof eaves and a gravel base that promotes drainage even when the ground is frozen. Furnace exhaust vents require similar vigilance\u2014high-efficiency systems vent through PVC pipes that can fill with ice when condensate freezes or snow blocks the termination.<\/p>\n\n<\/div><figure class=\"wp-block-media-text__media\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"1024\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez3-condenser.png\" alt=\"condenser - professional HVAC service photo\" class=\"wp-image-1794\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez3-condenser.png 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez3-condenser-300x300.png 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez3-condenser-150x150.png 150w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez3-condenser-768x768.png 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--ai\" title=\"AI-generated (gemini-2.5-flash-image)\">AI<\/span><\/figure><\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group alignfull s-band s-band--warm-gradient has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-08713647 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:6rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:6rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-cta has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\">\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Second floor stays ten degrees colder?<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">That is a duct design issue we measure and fix. Text us a photo of your thermostat and vents\u2014we will tell you what we see.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-buttons-is-layout-35f06ea7 wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"\/contact\/\">Send Photo &amp; Get Diagnosis<\/a><\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group alignfull s-band s-band--cream has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-08713647 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:6rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:6rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-element-heading has-text-align-center wp-block-heading\">Warren HVAC questions answered.<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-accordion s-accordion--bordered has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-1583283a wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\">\n<details class=\"wp-block-details is-layout-flow wp-block-details-is-layout-flow\"><summary>Do I need a backup heat source in Warren?<\/summary>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Strongly recommended. Power outages during ice storms can last days, and a gas furnace with no blower or heat pump with no electricity won&#039;t keep you warm. Options include a wood stove, propane space heater, or a generator sized to run essential circuits including the furnace blower. Battery backups work for short outages but won&#039;t sustain you through multi-day blackouts.<\/p>\n\n<\/details>\n\n\n\n<details class=\"wp-block-details is-layout-flow wp-block-details-is-layout-flow\"><summary>How often should I maintain my furnace here?<\/summary>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Annually at minimum, ideally before heating season starts. Warren furnaces run harder and longer than those in milder climates, accumulating more wear and carbon buildup. Neglecting maintenance leads to cracked heat exchangers, failed blowers, and mid-winter breakdowns when no contractor can respond quickly. A fall tuneup catches small issues before they become emergencies.<\/p>\n\n<\/details>\n\n\n\n<details class=\"wp-block-details is-layout-flow wp-block-details-is-layout-flow\"><summary>Can I install a ductless mini-split in Warren?<\/summary>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Yes, but choose a cold-climate model rated for sub-zero operation. Standard mini-splits lose heating capacity below twenty degrees and need backup heat. Cold-climate models maintain output to negative fifteen degrees or lower and work well in Warren if sized correctly. They are ideal for additions, finished basements, or homes without existing ductwork.<\/p>\n\n<\/details>\n\n\n\n<details class=\"wp-block-details is-layout-flow wp-block-details-is-layout-flow\"><summary>What&#039;s the design temperature Warren uses for sizing?<\/summary>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Around negative five degrees Fahrenheit\u2014roughly ten to fifteen degrees colder than state averages. That difference means furnaces must deliver their full rated output at that point, not at milder design conditions. Undersizing equipment based on generic Pennsylvania data leaves your home struggling during the coldest weeks when you need reliable heat most.<\/p>\n\n<\/details>\n\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-nearby has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\">\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Also serving nearby:<\/strong> <a href=\"\/deep-cold-answers-for-bradford-where-winter-means-it\/\">Bradford<\/a><\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;pa